  "live_records": {
    "q-113062": {
      "dom_id": "step-q113062",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Solve $f(x)=0$ where $f(x)=\\frac{x+5}{2{x}^{2}-5x-25}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we factor $f(x),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{x+5}{2{x}^{2}-5x-25} \\\\  & =\\frac{x+5}{(x-5)(2x+5)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we set the numerator equal to zero and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+5 & =0 \\\\ x & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to $f(x)=0$ is $x=-5.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
