    "q-25307": {
      "dom_id": "step-q25307",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Find the roots of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+3x-10}{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-9x+18}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The roots of $f(x)$ are the solutions to the equation $f(x)=0.$ In our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}+3x-10}{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-9x+18}=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+3x-10}{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-9x+18} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+5)(x-2)}{{x}^{2}(x-2)-9(x-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+5)(x-2)}{({x}^{2}-9)(x-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+5)(x-2)}{(x+3)(x-3)(x-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+5)\\cancel{(x-2)}}{(x+3)(x-3)\\cancel{(x-2)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+5)}{(x+3)(x-3)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the numerator equal to zero and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+5=0\\,⟹\\,x=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to $f(x)=0$ is $x=-5.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
